# Documented, scoped security exceptions - NOT a blanket suppression.
# Only the two CVE/GHSA IDs below are ignored; any other Trivy finding
# still fails the build (see .github/workflows/cd.yml).
#
# Both showed up identically across scans against python:3.11-slim-trixie
# AND python:3.11-slim-bookworm - two different Debian releases - with
# the exact same package versions (setuptools 70.3.0, msgpack 1.1.2) both
# times. That rules out a Debian-OS-shipped file (which would differ by
# release) and points to Python's own `ensurepip` bundled-wheel mechanism
# baked into the CPython 3.11.x build itself. The Dockerfile already
# strips /usr/local/lib/python3.11/ensurepip and Debian's separate
# /usr/share/python-wheels location; despite that, Trivy still detects
# these two specific versions somewhere in the image (Trivy can read a
# package version directly out of a .whl file without it being
# installed). Neither package is imported or executed by the running
# application - confirmed via `python -X importtime` and by tracing
# sys.modules through a live request (see README).
#
# ignore-unfixed does NOT suppress these, because both have a real fix
# available upstream (Status: fixed) - the CVEs just haven't been chased
# out of wherever this dormant copy lives yet.
#
# Revisit next time the base image or Python patch version changes.

# msgpack: MessagePack for Python - Out-of-bounds read / crash on
# Unpacker reuse. Vendored inside a bundled pip wheel, not a direct or
# transitive dependency this project installs. Fixed upstream in 1.2.1.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools: Path Traversal Vulnerability in setuptools PackageIndex.
# Same dormant bundled-wheel source. Fixed upstream in 78.1.1; the venv's
# own setuptools is already upgraded well past this (see Dockerfile).
CVE-2025-47273
